00:08:42.360 --> 00:08:44.100
and now I'm here teaching

00:08:44.100 --> 00:08:46.470
the full stack web development course.

00:08:46.470 --> 00:08:49.120
And with that, let's get started.

00:08:52.500 --> 00:08:53.880
All right let's have a look at

00:08:53.880 --> 00:08:56.110
what you will learn in this course.

00:08:56.110 --> 00:08:59.020
A couple of things I
already talked about, Svelte

00:08:59.020 --> 00:09:01.720
on the front end,
SvelteKit to build the API

00:09:01.720 --> 00:09:03.960
and host the web application,

00:09:03.960 --> 00:09:05.940
Postgres for the database

00:09:08.030 --> 00:09:10.100
Vercel to serve the website and the API

00:09:11.100 --> 00:09:13.970
and the Railway to host
the Postgres database.

00:09:13.970 --> 00:09:16.370
I talked about that before
so no change on that.

00:09:17.623 --> 00:09:22.490
In addition to all that,
we will look at TypeScript.

00:09:22.490 --> 00:09:24.210
So the reason that we're
going to use TypeScript

00:09:24.210 --> 00:09:29.210
is because I want to show
you a fully typed environment

00:09:29.460 --> 00:09:32.860
where we actually can use TypeScript

00:09:32.860 --> 00:09:36.810
and autocomplete for our database model.

00:09:36.810 --> 00:09:41.810
So if we have a database
model called todo-item,

00:09:42.150 --> 00:09:45.350
and that has a number of columns,

00:09:45.350 --> 00:09:49.170
we can then use that
autocomplete in TypeScript

00:09:49.170 --> 00:09:52.220
to access the values in these calls.

00:09:52.220 --> 00:09:56.360
This is all possible because
of Prisma, a tool that we are

00:09:56.360 --> 00:10:00.360
going to use in order
to generate these types

00:10:00.360 --> 00:10:01.990
based on a database schema.

00:10:01.990 --> 00:10:06.990
Now, Prisma will also help
us to run all the SQL queries

00:10:07.000 --> 00:10:09.030
and abstract all that from us.

00:10:09.030 --> 00:10:13.540
So even though we are using
SQL database, Postgres,

00:10:14.390 --> 00:10:18.610
we have not actually going
to write any SQL queries.

00:10:18.610 --> 00:10:21.060
It's really beautiful, you're
gonna absolutely love it,

00:10:21.060 --> 00:10:22.330
I can promise you.

00:10:22.330 --> 00:10:24.540
There will be an interface generated

00:10:24.540 --> 00:10:26.860
or a client generated by Prisma,

00:10:26.860 --> 00:10:28.910
where we can just use it with TypeScript,

00:10:29.990 --> 00:10:31.830
call functions on it,
and it will fetch data

00:10:31.830 --> 00:10:34.400
from the database, do all the SQL queries,

00:10:34.400 --> 00:10:35.880
conversions and all for us.

00:10:36.720 --> 00:10:40.730
The last thing we're going
to dive in is NPM scripts.

00:10:40.730 --> 00:10:43.830
You may have heard of tooling like gulp

00:10:43.830 --> 00:10:48.570
or other tools that help you glue together

00:10:48.570 --> 00:10:51.790
your development environment
and start, you know,

00:10:51.790 --> 00:10:55.700
dev servers and watch for file
changes and things like that.

00:10:56.880 --> 00:11:00.670
We will simplify that
in my personal opinion,

00:11:00.670 --> 00:11:05.010
by using NPM scripts and
basically have all the scripts

00:11:05.010 --> 00:11:06.210
that we need in order

00:11:06.210 --> 00:11:11.210
to test, deploy and
develop the application.

00:11:11.640 --> 00:11:15.980
This will all be part of
NPM scripts inside package,

00:11:15.980 --> 00:11:18.530
JSON file at the root of our project.

00:11:19.580 --> 00:11:21.940
This is at the high level,
what are we going to learn.

00:11:21.940 --> 00:11:23.650
You do not have to be an expert

00:11:23.650 --> 00:11:25.310
or even the beginning any of that,

00:11:25.310 --> 00:11:28.550
all you need to know is
basic JavaScript skills.

00:11:28.550 --> 00:11:31.170
The rest I will teach you as we go through

00:11:31.170 --> 00:11:33.090
and as it becomes necessary.

00:11:33.090 --> 00:11:36.450
So don't expect to be a TypeScript expert

00:11:36.450 --> 00:11:38.770
by the end of this course, however,

00:11:38.770 --> 00:11:41.940
if you have never heard of
TypeScript or have never used it,

00:11:41.940 --> 00:11:44.470
you will be just fine
going through this course.

00:11:44.470 --> 00:11:47.560
And I will guide you and
teach you everything you need

00:11:47.560 --> 00:11:50.570
to know in order to develop this project.

00:11:50.570 --> 00:11:52.130
The same is true for

00:11:52.130 --> 00:11:55.310
any of the other technologies
that we are going to be using.

00:11:55.310 --> 00:11:57.880
Fantastic, with that, this
gives you a good overview

00:11:57.880 --> 00:11:59.300
of what we're going to be learning.

