You can see we get an
array first and second.

03:08:04.190 --> 03:08:09.190
All we need to do is when
we load the index page,

03:08:11.640 --> 03:08:15.740
before we rendered a component
and before we even returned

03:08:15.740 --> 03:08:17.410
anything from the server,

03:08:17.410 --> 03:08:19.930
the server has to call
that todos endpoint,

03:08:19.930 --> 03:08:22.720
to fetch the existing elements,

03:08:22.720 --> 03:08:27.210
and then render one line per todo-item

03:08:27.210 --> 03:08:29.678
and then return all the HTML to the client

03:08:29.678 --> 03:08:31.890
so that the client doesn't have

03:08:31.890 --> 03:08:35.190
to make another HTTP
request to fetch the items.

03:08:35.190 --> 03:08:37.340
This is called server-side rendering

03:08:37.340 --> 03:08:39.390
and SvelteKit makes this super easy.

03:08:41.010 --> 03:08:42.160
Now, before we do that,

03:08:43.410 --> 03:08:48.410
we probably need to persist
more than just the string.

03:08:48.540 --> 03:08:53.030
Somehow we also need to know
whether the item is checked,

03:08:53.030 --> 03:08:54.680
so mark this done,

03:08:54.680 --> 03:08:57.660
and we also want to
probably keep some kind

03:08:57.660 --> 03:08:59.360
of date as to when it was created.

03:09:00.230 --> 03:09:01.830
So let's make this change first,

03:09:02.960 --> 03:09:07.470
and instead of persisting,
just a string here,

03:09:07.470 --> 03:09:10.800
we want a persistent
object or a todo item.

03:09:12.680 --> 03:09:17.650
Now, remember how we use
TypeScript here to help us navigate

03:09:18.720 --> 03:09:21.420
that code and implement autocomplete?

03:09:22.820 --> 03:09:27.820
Right now the todos array
can persist a string,

03:09:28.350 --> 03:09:32.020
but I could also, let me
just show you that real quick

03:09:33.080 --> 03:09:37.130
persist an object with a property text,

03:09:38.231 --> 03:09:40.610
that would work just fine.

03:09:40.610 --> 03:09:44.880
So this is okay, but we can do better.

03:09:44.880 --> 03:09:49.560
We can use TypeScript
to help us and ensure

03:09:49.560 --> 03:09:53.850
that we only persist the
correct type into this array.

03:09:55.200 --> 03:09:56.640
How does this work?

03:09:56.640 --> 03:09:58.810
Just like we used a request handler,

03:09:58.810 --> 03:10:03.090
we can create our own type for TypeScript,

03:10:03.090 --> 03:10:08.090
and then say that in this
array, we only want todo-items.

03:10:08.380 --> 03:10:10.250
So how do we do that in SvelteKit?

03:10:11.920 --> 03:10:13.750
You notice there's a file

03:10:13.750 --> 03:10:18.600
under source, SRC, global.d.ts

03:10:19.840 --> 03:10:21.600
If we open that up,

03:10:21.600 --> 03:10:26.600
we can define our to do type right here

03:10:26.960 --> 03:10:29.240
and it will be available to us

03:10:29.240 --> 03:10:32.970
across the entire application,
hence global.d.ts.

03:10:35.216 --> 03:10:37.330
D stands for the TypeScript Hence

03:10:37.330 --> 03:10:41.180
so what do we want to
do is we can say type,

03:10:42.260 --> 03:10:46.790
it will be a todo type equals,

03:10:46.790 --> 03:10:50.760
and don't get confused by these brackets.

03:10:50.760 --> 03:10:53.990
This is not a regular JavaScript object,

03:10:53.990 --> 03:10:58.990
it's a TypeScript type definition,
so we want a created at,

03:11:00.590 --> 03:11:02.610
and that will be a date.

03:11:04.000 --> 03:11:07.770
And we want a text, which is a string

03:11:10.060 --> 03:11:14.330
as well as a done,
which will be a Boolean.

03:11:15.350 --> 03:11:19.670
This is probably a good
start to kick things off

03:11:19.670 --> 03:11:24.670
and allow us to specify what
kind of type we want to store.

03:11:26.610 --> 03:11:30.470
So now, if I say that the array of todos,

03:11:31.410 --> 03:11:34.380
we can use to type here and say that, Hey,

03:11:34.380 --> 03:11:37.950
I only wanted todo-items
persisted in here,

03:11:37.950 --> 03:11:40.230
and this is an array of those.

03:11:41.860 --> 03:11:43.530
If we mouse over,

03:11:43.530 --> 03:11:47.550
you can see that this is
an array of todo types.

03:11:48.860 --> 03:11:50.090
Okay?

03:11:50.090 --> 03:11:53.040
So that's good, and you immediately notice

03:11:54.554 --> 03:11:58.320
at the bottom, it is complaining now.

03:11:59.590 --> 03:12:02.710
And if we mouse over that error,

03:12:02.710 --> 03:12:06.900
you can see that type text string,

03:12:06.900 --> 03:12:11.900
which is our text request
body get texts, this line.

03:12:12.170 --> 03:12:14.550
So that type is missing
the following properties

03:12:14.550 --> 03:12:17.690
from the type todo, created at and done.

03:12:18.920 --> 03:12:20.690
Interesting, let's have a look.

03:12:21.890 --> 03:12:26.770
If we were to use
autocomplete, huh, that's cool.

03:12:26.770 --> 03:12:29.710
It is telling us that
there's two more properties

03:12:29.710 --> 03:12:31.570
that we need to specify.

03:12:31.570 --> 03:12:36.180
One is created at, and that's
just a new date right now.

03:12:37.460 --> 03:12:39.410
And then I think there was another one.

03:12:40.810 --> 03:12:41.970
Let's do that again,

03:12:41.970 --> 03:12:45.610
yeah, there's done as well and done,

03:12:45.610 --> 03:12:47.830
when we create the new todo-item,

03:12:47.830 --> 03:12:51.870
then done is false to start with.

03:12:54.200 --> 03:12:56.444
Now TypeScript is satisfied

03:12:56.444 --> 03:13:00.113
because we are now
creating a proper todo-item

03:13:00.113 --> 03:13:03.450
with a created at, a text and a done,

03:13:03.450 --> 03:13:05.200
it's no longer complaining

03:13:05.200 --> 03:13:08.500
that we cannot push that
into the produce array.

03:13:08.500 --> 03:13:10.280
So this is pretty good.

03:13:10.280 --> 03:13:13.860
Now we know whatever element
is in this todos array

03:13:13.860 --> 03:13:16.880
is of type todo, and it has
three properties defined.

03:13:18.900 --> 03:13:21.450
We're making good progress.

03:13:21.450 --> 03:13:24.890
What's still missing though is

03:13:26.068 --> 03:13:29.990
the fact that it's not
actually showing our items.

03:13:29.990 --> 03:13:34.660
So as I said, we need to load
all the existing todo-items

03:13:34.660 --> 03:13:37.340
when we request that page from the server.

03:13:38.730 --> 03:13:43.090
We can do that in the index.Svelte file.

03:13:46.000 --> 03:13:47.550
What we have to do is,

03:13:47.550 --> 03:13:50.650
and that's well documented
in the SvelteKit docs,

03:13:50.650 --> 03:13:55.650
but besides the script tag that we have,

03:13:56.940 --> 03:14:01.490
we have to create another
tag, another element.

03:14:01.490 --> 03:14:03.330
It's also a script,

03:14:03.330 --> 03:14:06.220
but it is a little bit
more special than that

03:14:06.220 --> 03:14:10.670
because it has context equals module.

03:14:12.620 --> 03:14:17.030
So this is how you can
differentiate the two.

03:14:18.540 --> 03:14:21.570
Every time a component gets rendered,

03:14:21.570 --> 03:14:26.460
this script gets executed
and the script module

03:14:26.460 --> 03:14:31.300
only gets executed once
across all the instances,

03:14:31.300 --> 03:14:32.976
but this is the place where

03:14:32.976 --> 03:14:36.422
if you're familiar with
like Next.js or others,

03:14:36.422 --> 03:14:37.860
where you would call,

03:14:37.860 --> 03:14:42.230
like get the initial
props or places like that,

03:14:42.230 --> 03:14:44.940
where you can fetch data
from the server before

03:14:44.940 --> 03:14:48.850
the component is rendered,
this is what we want to do,

03:14:48.850 --> 03:14:50.600
and because we're using TypeScript,

03:14:52.070 --> 03:14:57.070
we can tell that script that
we will use TypeScript within.

03:14:57.440 --> 03:15:00.460
So we can say language is TypeScript.

03:15:02.790 --> 03:15:07.230
The convention here is
that we need to export

03:15:07.230 --> 03:15:09.200
a function called load

03:15:09.200 --> 03:15:12.840
that SvelteKit will automatically call

03:15:12.840 --> 03:15:14.960
as part of the server side rendering.

03:15:15.950 --> 03:15:17.660
So let's export that function,

03:15:19.361 --> 03:15:24.361
const load a regular function.

03:15:26.410 --> 03:15:27.570
It's a good start.

03:15:27.570 --> 03:15:30.760
And we want to leverage
TypeScript here as well

03:15:30.760 --> 03:15:35.760
to help us with the parameters
that are being passed in

03:15:35.960 --> 03:15:37.850
and kind of the return values we have

03:15:38.710 --> 03:15:40.690
to specify from this function.

03:15:40.690 --> 03:15:42.230
So at the top here,

03:15:42.230 --> 03:15:46.490
we can import a type
and it is called load.

03:15:46.490 --> 03:15:51.030
We grabbed that from
the SvelteKit package,

03:15:53.160 --> 03:15:57.630
and then we can annotate this
load function by saying load

03:15:58.880 --> 03:16:03.880
and just like that, we can now
see what we need to return.

03:16:03.950 --> 03:16:08.950
So if we say return and
we use autocomplete,

03:16:09.196 --> 03:16:10.890
there's some error,

03:16:10.890 --> 03:16:14.880
maxage, props, other stuff in here.

03:16:14.880 --> 03:16:19.280
So eventually we'll specify
the right things here,

03:16:19.280 --> 03:16:24.170
but thanks to this TypeScript
type that we specified,

03:16:24.170 --> 03:16:27.070
we are not able to see
these autocomplete items.

03:16:29.250 --> 03:16:30.960
So one other thing we want

03:16:30.960 --> 03:16:35.960
is at this point, this is
where we want to fetch the data

03:16:36.150 --> 03:16:38.650
from the backend API, right?

03:16:38.650 --> 03:16:43.650
Remember from the slash todos.JSON,

03:16:45.260 --> 03:16:48.600
it's empty now because we
restarted the server automatically

03:16:48.600 --> 03:16:52.640
when we made code changes
there and our array got erased

03:16:52.640 --> 03:16:55.980
from memory, but we want
to call that endpoint,

03:16:55.980 --> 03:17:00.320
get that array, and then
render each array item in here.

03:17:01.940 --> 03:17:06.940
Okay, the way we do that is we
get an object as a parameter.

03:17:07.430 --> 03:17:09.490
And one of the values

03:17:09.490 --> 03:17:12.720
in there, or one of the
properties is called fetch.

03:17:12.720 --> 03:17:14.850
If we use that fetch, not to confuse

03:17:14.850 --> 03:17:18.390
that with the regular fetch
that you get in the browser,

03:17:18.390 --> 03:17:22.120
this is a special fetch
that's provided by SvelteKit.

03:17:22.120 --> 03:17:24.520
So always make sure you use that.

03:17:26.060 --> 03:17:29.910
This is where we can now
call that endpoint to get

03:17:29.910 --> 03:17:34.910
and fetch our todos, so
fetch slash todos.JSON.

03:17:37.810 --> 03:17:42.110
And this is an async call,
so it's returning a promise.

03:17:42.110 --> 03:17:44.990
So let's change our function

03:17:47.005 --> 03:17:50.210
to async and then leverage a wait here.

03:17:50.210 --> 03:17:55.210
So the response is a wait fetch.

03:17:57.210 --> 03:18:02.020
Now, if the response is okay, again,

03:18:02.020 --> 03:18:05.170
you can see TypeScript
helping us here, if it's okay,

03:18:06.960 --> 03:18:10.670
then where you want to
convert the response

03:18:10.670 --> 03:18:12.430
and get these todo-items out of it,

03:18:15.029 --> 03:18:19.410
so todos equals await,
JSON response there.

03:18:19.410 --> 03:18:24.410
Now that array contains the
same elements as that array

03:18:24.740 --> 03:18:28.200
because we return it as part
of the party in this get

03:18:28.200 --> 03:18:31.690
request, which we call with
the fetch function here.

03:18:33.100 --> 03:18:33.933
All right.

03:18:35.290 --> 03:18:36.510
Having these todo-items,

03:18:37.557 --> 03:18:39.580
we need to pass them to our component,

03:18:39.580 --> 03:18:43.300
so that down here, instead
of rendering three static

03:18:43.300 --> 03:18:47.170
todo-items, we want to render
X amount of todo-items,

03:18:47.170 --> 03:18:49.720
depending on how many have
been added to the array.

03:18:52.010 --> 03:18:57.010
So if we use TypeScript autocomplete here,

03:18:57.980 --> 03:19:01.500
you see one property is called props,

03:19:01.500 --> 03:19:02.930
and that's exactly what we want to do.

03:19:02.930 --> 03:19:04.890
We want to use the props

03:19:04.890 --> 03:19:07.280
to be passed into that component here.

03:19:08.290 --> 03:19:13.290
So props is an object and we
just want to pass in the todos

03:19:14.430 --> 03:19:19.110
which creates a todos property

03:19:19.110 --> 03:19:22.390
that is being passed into the script.

03:19:22.390 --> 03:19:25.480
So we can come here and I'll teach you

03:19:25.480 --> 03:19:27.940
how to do props in Svelte.

03:19:29.070 --> 03:19:31.390
The way it works is the syntax for that

03:19:32.441 --> 03:19:34.770
is export let todos.

03:19:37.330 --> 03:19:41.850
That gives us a prop called todo

03:19:41.850 --> 03:19:43.980
that's exported from this component

03:19:43.980 --> 03:19:48.040
so here is where we specify the props

03:19:48.040 --> 03:19:50.120
we want to pass in down here.

03:19:51.110 --> 03:19:52.760
You can see that it's complaining

03:19:53.667 --> 03:19:55.680
that we don't have type defined.

03:19:55.680 --> 03:19:59.720
So we actually have the to do type right,

03:19:59.720 --> 03:20:01.600
that we created in global.TS.

03:20:03.570 --> 03:20:05.930
So we know that this property is going

03:20:05.930 --> 03:20:07.930
to be of type todo, so we can say,

03:20:09.380 --> 03:20:12.470
this will be an array of todo-items.

03:20:12.470 --> 03:20:14.370
And because we know using TypeScript,

03:20:15.280 --> 03:20:20.140
we have to let the script
know that we use TypeScript.

03:20:21.960 --> 03:20:24.070
All right, that was a lot,

03:20:24.070 --> 03:20:29.070
but basically we exported a
load function that executes

03:20:29.370 --> 03:20:31.830
on the server when we
do a full page refresh,

03:20:31.830 --> 03:20:33.870
which is currently the case.

03:20:33.870 --> 03:20:35.100
If we were to navigate

03:20:35.100 --> 03:20:39.433
from one page to another,
then the client side would,

03:20:40.710 --> 03:20:42.490
the browser would call this load function

03:20:42.490 --> 03:20:44.870
and do a client side fetch.

03:20:44.870 --> 03:20:48.660
But in our case, because we
always refresh that page,

03:20:48.660 --> 03:20:52.360
ignore that error, because
we all just reload the page,

03:20:52.360 --> 03:20:55.140
that fetch actually
executes on the server,

03:20:55.140 --> 03:20:57.240
the load function, and then calling fetch.

03:20:58.440 --> 03:21:03.440
So we go grab that and we
return if everything is okay.

03:21:06.510 --> 03:21:09.750
We passed the todos array into here,

03:21:09.750 --> 03:21:13.100
and then we currently
not using it anywhere.

03:21:13.100 --> 03:21:15.390
So it's giving us a little warning.

03:21:15.390 --> 03:21:17.940
We will do that in a second,
but before we move on,

03:21:18.900 --> 03:21:22.270
let's deal with the error case
in case something goes wrong

03:21:22.270 --> 03:21:25.510
with our fetch, what we can say is

03:21:26.980 --> 03:21:29.680
if the response is okay,
we return, so that means

03:21:29.680 --> 03:21:33.740
that down here on line 13,
the response was not okay.

03:21:33.740 --> 03:21:36.590
So what we can do is we
can fetch the message

03:21:39.490 --> 03:21:44.490
and we do that from
await response, dot text.

03:21:50.330 --> 03:21:54.140
So basically, oops, that should be JSON.

03:21:55.160 --> 03:21:58.560
So basically whatever we
get back from the server,

03:21:58.560 --> 03:22:01.000
it will contain a message
object, we haven't built

03:22:01.000 --> 03:22:04.490
that yet, but that's just
preparing us for later.

03:22:05.350 --> 03:22:08.563
And then what we want
to do is we don't want

03:22:08.563 --> 03:22:11.650
to return props because
if we return props,

03:22:11.650 --> 03:22:13.860
we indicate that everything was okay,

03:22:15.207 --> 03:22:18.830
so we can return an error.

03:22:19.910 --> 03:22:21.570
And that's just a new error

03:22:22.490 --> 03:22:24.240
with the message that we receive.

03:22:25.530 --> 03:22:27.610
The nice thing about
that is that if we return

03:22:27.610 --> 03:22:30.770
an error then the SvelteKit
will automatically render

03:22:30.770 --> 03:22:32.990
an error page instead of our component.

03:22:34.330 --> 03:22:35.163
Alrighty.

03:22:37.940 --> 03:22:42.630
We now have the todos array
that contains whatever elements

03:22:42.630 --> 03:22:45.390
are in the array on the server side.

03:22:46.260 --> 03:22:47.830
Now we have to use that

03:22:47.830 --> 03:22:52.830
to render todo-items
depending on how many we have.

03:22:54.710 --> 03:22:57.270
So basically we need a for loop

03:23:00.040 --> 03:23:03.480
or in Svelte's case, an each loop.

03:23:03.480 --> 03:23:07.410
This index for that is that you
use the open curly brackets,

03:23:07.410 --> 03:23:10.290
hashtag each,

03:23:10.290 --> 03:23:14.570
and then you specify which
array we are iterating over.

03:23:14.570 --> 03:23:15.900
So that's our todos array.

03:23:16.790 --> 03:23:18.690
And then what's the variable name

03:23:20.065 --> 03:23:23.646
of the individual todo-item of this array,

03:23:23.646 --> 03:23:28.000
so as todo allows us to
access to individual item

03:23:28.000 --> 03:23:32.040
from the array, with the
variable to do, and then

03:23:33.021 --> 03:23:37.147
to close it, curly brackets
slash each closes the loop.

03:23:38.060 --> 03:23:41.290
Now it's telling us this
is an empty each block,

03:23:41.290 --> 03:23:42.340
please don't do that,

03:23:43.540 --> 03:23:47.680
that's fine we can have
that todo-item render

03:23:47.680 --> 03:23:52.010
and we do not need these
other two items we have there.

03:23:53.590 --> 03:23:54.490
Let's have a look.

03:23:56.660 --> 03:24:00.310
Nothing rendered because
we have nothing added yet.

03:24:00.310 --> 03:24:02.390
We go to first.

03:24:04.820 --> 03:24:08.155
And we now have one item in the array.

03:24:08.155 --> 03:24:10.190
It doesn't show anything,

03:24:10.190 --> 03:24:13.410
and I'll show you that in
a minute, how we fix it,

03:24:13.410 --> 03:24:14.460
let's do another one.

03:24:16.970 --> 03:24:17.803
Two items, nice.

03:24:18.960 --> 03:24:21.608
It doesn't show any texts or anything

03:24:21.608 --> 03:24:24.970
because we still just render a todo item

03:24:24.970 --> 03:24:29.690
that if we look at the details
under source lib todo-item

03:24:30.610 --> 03:24:33.260
in the HTML, it doesn't
literally do anything,

03:24:33.260 --> 03:24:37.770
it's all empty, that's why we
just see two empty elements.

03:24:38.830 --> 03:24:39.830
So first things first,

03:24:39.830 --> 03:24:44.830
we need to pass this
todo-item into the component.

03:24:46.920 --> 03:24:50.810
And remember in Svelte, export let

03:24:50.810 --> 03:24:54.180
is how you specify a prop

03:24:55.050 --> 03:24:58.770
so we can do the same for the todo-item.

03:25:00.070 --> 03:25:03.290
So up at the top, we
don't have a script yet,

03:25:03.290 --> 03:25:06.210
we add script.

03:25:09.240 --> 03:25:12.540
We also want to use the TypeScript here.

03:25:12.540 --> 03:25:17.487
So language TS, and we say export let

03:25:19.670 --> 03:25:23.010
a single todo of type todo.

03:25:25.120 --> 03:25:28.310
And we get a warning because
we're not using it yet.

03:25:28.310 --> 03:25:30.360
That is changing right now.

03:25:30.360 --> 03:25:32.880
The only thing we have for
now is the text property,

03:25:32.880 --> 03:25:37.680
remember in the API post,
we set the created at,

03:25:37.680 --> 03:25:41.750
which we don't display in
the UI, where you set a text,

03:25:41.750 --> 03:25:45.470
which is the value we entered
and had done, that's false,

03:25:45.470 --> 03:25:47.190
in the todo-item.

