functionality that we need.

03:44:22.170 --> 03:44:27.170
Now, if we have a look in both cases here,

03:44:27.720 --> 03:44:31.960
we eventually return that object.

03:44:31.960 --> 03:44:34.760
So that depends, the value of that object,

03:44:34.760 --> 03:44:38.940
the return object depends on
whether we do a post or a get.

03:44:38.940 --> 03:44:41.260
So I suggest we will move that code also

03:44:41.260 --> 03:44:44.850
into the API so that in this file here,

03:44:46.370 --> 03:44:50.950
we can just make a call to
the API and return the result.

03:44:50.950 --> 03:44:54.150
So we don't have to do
any more code in here.

03:44:55.500 --> 03:45:00.500
Let's start by running a switch statement.

03:45:01.570 --> 03:45:05.520
So switch and the value we want to check,

03:45:05.520 --> 03:45:07.880
as I mentioned is request.method,

03:45:09.910 --> 03:45:13.960
which is going to be either
post or get or patch,

03:45:13.960 --> 03:45:16.190
things like that, as we go through.

03:45:17.440 --> 03:45:21.120
Now, let's also make this uppercase

03:45:22.020 --> 03:45:25.600
just to be sure in case it
is being sent by clients

03:45:25.600 --> 03:45:29.190
in different format, lowercase
or uppercase mixed maybe.

03:45:29.190 --> 03:45:34.190
Now the value we want
to look for here is get.

03:45:36.610 --> 03:45:40.970
In the get case, we want to
return all these todo-items.

03:45:40.970 --> 03:45:44.200
And in order to do that, remember here,

03:45:44.200 --> 03:45:49.200
we had a body and a status
of 200 and the todo-items.

03:45:51.230 --> 03:45:52.598
So what we can do in here in our API,

03:45:52.598 --> 03:45:54.560
above the switch statement,

03:45:55.470 --> 03:46:00.470
we can specify a body and
that's by default empty.

03:46:01.050 --> 03:46:06.000
And we can specify a status
that is by default 500.

03:46:06.000 --> 03:46:07.500
Now we set this to 500,

03:46:07.500 --> 03:46:10.530
which represents an internal server error,

03:46:10.530 --> 03:46:14.630
just so that if somebody sends a request

03:46:15.530 --> 03:46:19.050
with a method that we did not
add to our switch statement,

03:46:19.050 --> 03:46:21.540
the default behavior will be a 500 error,

03:46:22.400 --> 03:46:25.780
which indicates that
whatever the clients try

03:46:25.780 --> 03:46:28.870
to do with their method
here is not implemented yet,

03:46:28.870 --> 03:46:32.660
so right now, if somebody
were to send a post request,

03:46:32.660 --> 03:46:35.630
they would get a 500 error,
as soon as we returned that.

03:46:37.470 --> 03:46:39.090
Now, in the case of get,

03:46:40.340 --> 03:46:45.340
we know that the body has
to be the array of elements.

03:46:47.670 --> 03:46:50.560
We had that over here previously.

03:46:50.560 --> 03:46:52.840
Now we no longer have
the array here, however,

03:46:52.840 --> 03:46:55.710
we do have it here in our API.

03:46:55.710 --> 03:47:00.200
So we can say body equals todos

03:47:01.748 --> 03:47:03.430
and status equals 200.

03:47:04.480 --> 03:47:07.100
With that we rebuild the functionality

03:47:07.100 --> 03:47:09.680
that we had in the index.JSON.TS file.

03:47:11.470 --> 03:47:14.990
Lastly what we want to do

03:47:14.990 --> 03:47:16.860
after the switch statement

03:47:18.060 --> 03:47:23.060
is we want to return
that status and the body

03:47:27.620 --> 03:47:30.890
so that whatever we set
in the switch statement

03:47:30.890 --> 03:47:32.920
will get returned down here.

03:47:37.754 --> 03:47:39.490
Now, for the post request.

03:47:40.420 --> 03:47:42.240
So first of all, before
we get to the post,

03:47:42.240 --> 03:47:44.220
let's clean up the get request.

03:47:44.220 --> 03:47:49.220
And the way we do that is by
importing the API we created.

03:47:51.320 --> 03:47:54.900
So we can say import API

03:47:57.281 --> 03:47:59.920
from the API file.

03:48:01.220 --> 03:48:04.660
And then the fix down here,

03:48:04.660 --> 03:48:08.320
the code change is that
instead of just returning

03:48:08.320 --> 03:48:11.070
that object, we can remove that

03:48:13.543 --> 03:48:17.140
and we do need to get the request

03:48:17.140 --> 03:48:19.460
because our API expects that.

03:48:19.460 --> 03:48:24.460
And then we can say return
API and pass the request.

03:48:25.980 --> 03:48:29.520
Now this just becomes a
one-line function here

03:48:29.520 --> 03:48:32.410
where we call that API
that we specified here,

03:48:33.370 --> 03:48:38.370
then the switch statement
will fall into the get case

03:48:38.800 --> 03:48:41.450
where we set the body and the status,

03:48:41.450 --> 03:48:46.340
and down here, we return
body and status back,

03:48:46.340 --> 03:48:48.950
which then gets returned
from this function,

03:48:48.950 --> 03:48:52.860
and we are back to the
behavior we had previously.

03:48:54.090 --> 03:48:56.340
The benefit now is that
everything is consolidated

03:48:56.340 --> 03:48:57.520
in that API script.

03:48:58.500 --> 03:49:02.170
Let's do the same with the post endpoint.

03:49:02.170 --> 03:49:07.170
So in the switch statement,
let's add a case for post.

03:49:14.480 --> 03:49:18.530
So don't forget the break statement,

03:49:18.530 --> 03:49:20.930
otherwise we'll run into the next case

03:49:20.930 --> 03:49:24.450
and that will have
unexpected consequences.

03:49:26.280 --> 03:49:28.608
Okay, in the post case,

03:49:28.608 --> 03:49:30.058
let's see what we have to do.

03:49:30.990 --> 03:49:35.990
We need to push a new
item into the todos array,

03:49:37.700 --> 03:49:38.800
just like we did here.

03:49:39.770 --> 03:49:44.770
So we could potentially create that

03:49:46.710 --> 03:49:50.920
item inside of our API right here,

03:49:50.920 --> 03:49:53.160
by reading the values from the request.

03:49:54.080 --> 03:49:56.190
Another way to do that

03:49:57.220 --> 03:50:02.220
is to add a parameter to the API,

03:50:02.850 --> 03:50:05.270
which is a todo-item.

03:50:05.270 --> 03:50:08.670
And that will then basically

03:50:09.715 --> 03:50:13.980
help us create the item for the array.

03:50:13.980 --> 03:50:15.650
So either way it works.

03:50:15.650 --> 03:50:19.000
I think for now, what
we can do is right here,

03:50:19.000 --> 03:50:24.000
we'll create the item and then
we will pass it into the API.

03:50:24.060 --> 03:50:29.060
So let's say that our API
also requires a todo-item.

03:50:31.090 --> 03:50:33.860
And the type of that is
to do remember we created

03:50:33.860 --> 03:50:38.430
that in the global.d.ts,
there's our todo type,

03:50:38.430 --> 03:50:41.130
so we can tell what properties we expect.

03:50:44.320 --> 03:50:48.077
Now in the post scenario, we want to add,

03:50:50.830 --> 03:50:55.550
so push the todo-item into that array

03:50:55.550 --> 03:50:59.050
and then the body and status,

03:50:59.050 --> 03:51:04.050
in the post case, we can
go grab that from here,

03:51:04.100 --> 03:51:09.100
you'll see it was status 303
and headers and location.

03:51:10.830 --> 03:51:14.240
So this is interesting because

03:51:17.214 --> 03:51:19.950
that return object is different

03:51:19.950 --> 03:51:23.520
from the return object
that we had down here.

03:51:24.730 --> 03:51:26.970
Now for the time being,

03:51:28.648 --> 03:51:31.170
let's just take that return here.

03:51:34.350 --> 03:51:36.420
And because we're working

03:51:36.420 --> 03:51:41.340
on a post, we can come here and exit early

03:51:41.340 --> 03:51:44.410
to return that status 303

03:51:44.410 --> 03:51:46.940
because we don't really
want to return the body

03:51:46.940 --> 03:51:51.330
that we don't have, also
we need the headers object

03:51:51.330 --> 03:51:53.510
for the post request.

03:51:53.510 --> 03:51:55.920
So we don't want to, you know,

03:51:55.920 --> 03:51:58.690
deal with that down here
where sometimes the headers

03:51:58.690 --> 03:52:00.870
is available, sometimes it's not,

03:52:00.870 --> 03:52:03.090
we'll just move it in
here for the time being.

03:52:05.720 --> 03:52:08.230
All right, now, if we go
back to that index file,

03:52:10.340 --> 03:52:15.340
what do we want to do now, here
is basically call that API.

03:52:17.090 --> 03:52:18.340
So same as we did above,

03:52:18.340 --> 03:52:20.960
and we'll fix that
error there in a second.

03:52:20.960 --> 03:52:24.660
So again, we want to return API.

03:52:24.660 --> 03:52:29.220
The first parameter is a
request and the second one

03:52:29.220 --> 03:52:34.220
is the object that
represents our todo-item.

03:52:37.140 --> 03:52:39.590
And then we don't need
any of this anymore.

03:52:41.880 --> 03:52:43.060
So that's good.

03:52:44.410 --> 03:52:47.870
Now we noticed that the
return statement up here,

03:52:47.870 --> 03:52:50.785
where we call the API and to get request

03:52:50.785 --> 03:52:53.120
is now red underlined.

03:52:53.120 --> 03:52:56.510
And if we do that it says
that it expected two arguments

03:52:56.510 --> 03:52:59.250
but it got one, that's because we added

03:52:59.250 --> 03:53:02.450
that todo-item for the post requests,

03:53:02.450 --> 03:53:06.220
but when we have a get
request or maybe later

03:53:06.220 --> 03:53:09.310
delete request, we don't
really have a todo-item.

03:53:10.310 --> 03:53:15.310
So what we can do in TypeScript
is after the parameter name,

03:53:15.340 --> 03:53:17.240
we can add a question mark

03:53:18.890 --> 03:53:21.390
to mark this specific
parameter as optional.

03:53:22.230 --> 03:53:26.920
And now the API accepts a request

03:53:26.920 --> 03:53:29.460
or a request with a new todo-item.

03:53:31.440 --> 03:53:35.660
So so far we have refactored the code

03:53:35.660 --> 03:53:38.443
that we had previously,
the get and the post,

03:53:38.443 --> 03:53:40.490
and because we have return statement here,

03:53:40.490 --> 03:53:43.430
we don't really need the break,
we can remove that for now.

03:53:44.970 --> 03:53:47.130
Now we did all that work

03:53:47.130 --> 03:53:49.450
because we wanted to
add a delete endpoint.

03:53:50.930 --> 03:53:53.280
So we have the wrapper here

03:53:53.280 --> 03:53:56.120
and now what we can do
in that specific file,

03:53:57.010 --> 03:54:02.010
we can leverage what we
already built in the API file.

03:54:02.250 --> 03:54:05.220
So if we import the API here

03:54:06.690 --> 03:54:09.010
and that lives in that API file,

03:54:10.580 --> 03:54:15.230
we want this to be a return API request.

03:54:16.750 --> 03:54:18.850
And then we want the API file

03:54:18.850 --> 03:54:21.500
to worry about the details
of how to implement that.

03:54:24.640 --> 03:54:27.350
The way we do that is when
we have a delete request,

03:54:28.420 --> 03:54:33.420
we expect the HTTP method
to be delete, right?

03:54:34.690 --> 03:54:37.280
So we have get, post,

03:54:38.130 --> 03:54:42.460
and now we want a case

03:54:45.440 --> 03:54:47.150
for the delete endpoint.

03:54:49.710 --> 03:54:53.270
And I want a break from that.

03:54:54.630 --> 03:54:59.630
The response status for a delete request

03:55:00.520 --> 03:55:04.980
is going to be 200, so status 200.

03:55:04.980 --> 03:55:09.300
We do not have to specify
a body for a delete request

03:55:09.300 --> 03:55:12.770
because the item gets
removed and doesn't exist.

03:55:12.770 --> 03:55:15.040
So we'll keep the default, which

03:55:15.040 --> 03:55:19.670
is an empty object, but
we have to remove the item

03:55:21.852 --> 03:55:26.520
based on the UID from the
array that we have up here.

03:55:27.430 --> 03:55:30.690
Eventually when we have a
database, that will be super easy,

03:55:30.690 --> 03:55:34.580
we just say, you know, delete
from the database with that ID

03:55:35.600 --> 03:55:38.900
for now, because we just persist
that todos array in memory,

03:55:40.200 --> 03:55:44.620
we have to manually just go
in and filter the existing

03:55:44.620 --> 03:55:49.610
array, but not include the
element that we want to delete.

03:55:49.610 --> 03:55:50.520
So the way we do that

03:55:50.520 --> 03:55:54.970
is todos, we set a new value for that.

03:55:54.970 --> 03:55:56.690
And then we basically filter,

03:56:00.120 --> 03:56:03.630
we filter that and we say that we want

03:56:04.694 --> 03:56:08.560
the todo.UID not equals to

03:56:10.362 --> 03:56:14.967
remember request.params.UID
gives us the unique ID.

03:56:17.380 --> 03:56:21.750
And what we notice is that
an individual todo-item

03:56:21.750 --> 03:56:25.180
does not have a UID because at the moment,

03:56:25.180 --> 03:56:27.930
if we look at that global.d.ts file,

03:56:28.950 --> 03:56:31.980
there is no UID specified.

03:56:31.980 --> 03:56:36.980
However, because we need that
UID now to identify an item,

03:56:39.580 --> 03:56:43.703
we have to extend our todo
type by adding a UID property.

03:56:44.980 --> 03:56:46.530
And that will just be a string.

03:56:47.630 --> 03:56:52.630
So UID now exists and our
API no longer complains

03:56:52.900 --> 03:56:55.660
about the UID not being present.

03:56:56.660 --> 03:56:59.910
However, if we look at
the index JSON file,

03:57:01.130 --> 03:57:03.360
we know we're getting an
error here because we create

03:57:03.360 --> 03:57:08.360
a todo-item that does not
include a UID property.

03:57:08.410 --> 03:57:10.850
Now this is again, the beauty

03:57:10.850 --> 03:57:15.280
of TypeScript, really to help us identify

03:57:15.280 --> 03:57:18.740
these kind of box before
we even go to production.

03:57:20.030 --> 03:57:21.820
So what do we do?

03:57:21.820 --> 03:57:26.400
There's a good way, and a
temporary way to do that.

03:57:27.410 --> 03:57:30.720
The good way would be
to import a UUID package

03:57:32.060 --> 03:57:37.060
and create an actual UUID, or
we can do a little workaround,

03:57:38.400 --> 03:57:40.180
which is fine for now,

03:57:40.180 --> 03:57:44.010
but eventually that UID
will be generated for us

03:57:44.010 --> 03:57:46.980
by the database, so we really just

03:57:46.980 --> 03:57:48.830
add a temporary UID for now.

03:57:48.830 --> 03:57:53.650
And what we can do is UID
equals, it has to be a string.

03:57:53.650 --> 03:57:56.230
We specified it as a string type.

03:57:56.230 --> 03:58:00.460
So we can use string literals
here and say Date.now,

03:58:01.400 --> 03:58:03.760
which gives us the milliseconds

03:58:03.760 --> 03:58:05.890
when this item gets created.

03:58:05.890 --> 03:58:08.150
Again, don't do that in production,

03:58:08.150 --> 03:58:09.180
definitely don't do that

03:58:09.180 --> 03:58:12.490
if you have two requests
coming in at the same time,

03:58:12.490 --> 03:58:17.490
you will have a conflict of
two items with the same UID.

03:58:17.750 --> 03:58:19.000
So do not do that.

03:58:20.883 --> 03:58:24.343
Todo replace with UID from database.

03:58:32.110 --> 03:58:36.610
This is something that we will
fix once the database exists

03:58:36.610 --> 03:58:39.950
and we can create the item in the DB,

03:58:41.360 --> 03:58:44.010
but for now, at least we get a UID.

03:58:44.010 --> 03:58:46.560
And when we delete the item,

03:58:46.560 --> 03:58:49.670
we have access to that
and we can remove it.

03:58:51.780 --> 03:58:55.480
So this is a pretty good start.

03:58:56.440 --> 03:58:59.200
Now, what do we want to do next is

03:58:59.200 --> 03:59:02.040
go have a look at what
do we have to change

03:59:02.040 --> 03:59:06.970
in the UI in order to
call this delete endpoint.

03:59:09.430 --> 03:59:12.140
The place where we click the delete icon

03:59:13.040 --> 03:59:15.720
is under lib todo-item.

03:59:17.060 --> 03:59:18.520
In here, you know,

03:59:18.520 --> 03:59:20.740
that we have a prop
for our individual todo

03:59:21.610 --> 03:59:25.490
and down in the forms, you can see here,

03:59:25.490 --> 03:59:30.290
we have the delete todo button.

03:59:30.290 --> 03:59:35.160
Now the action is the
endpoint that we just created.

03:59:35.160 --> 03:59:40.160
So that endpoint lives
at slash todos slash

03:59:40.320 --> 03:59:41.740
let's just make UID.JSON.

03:59:44.530 --> 03:59:48.470
The UID has to be dynamic
depending on the item we render.

03:59:48.470 --> 03:59:51.100
So if you recall with the curly brackets,

03:59:51.100 --> 03:59:53.130
we can access the variables.

03:59:53.980 --> 03:59:56.650
So we can remove that and
just say curly brackets

03:59:58.642 --> 04:00:02.640
and todo.UID again, thanks to TypeScript,

04:00:02.640 --> 04:00:05.630
we have that autocomplete
of the new field available.

04:00:07.080 --> 04:00:12.080
And as we set the method
that we want to use,

04:00:12.590 --> 04:00:17.370
we'll look at the API, deleting
something in a REST API

04:00:17.370 --> 04:00:20.540
is an HTTP request with
a method of delete.

04:00:21.550 --> 04:00:24.560
So in our todo-item method,

04:00:24.560 --> 04:00:29.560
we want to say delete so that
the API knows what to do.

04:00:32.610 --> 04:00:36.380
Now, let's have a look
at the user interface.

04:00:36.380 --> 04:00:41.280
So we'd go back to the index
and there seems to be a bug

04:00:42.920 --> 04:00:44.630
somewhere, let's have a look okay.

04:00:45.990 --> 04:00:50.480
Just temporarily because
of the changes we made.

04:00:50.480 --> 04:00:54.870
Okay, let's clear this, clear console

04:00:54.870 --> 04:00:55.970
and let's add an item.

04:00:58.640 --> 04:01:00.070
So that worked.

04:01:00.070 --> 04:01:04.240
And now if we inspect
the button real quick,

04:01:05.580 --> 04:01:10.580
you can see that the form now
points to slash todos slash

04:01:11.050 --> 04:01:13.420
the unique ID that we created

04:01:13.420 --> 04:01:16.725
based on the date dot
now function dot JSON.

04:01:16.725 --> 04:01:18.480
So this is just like before,

04:01:18.480 --> 04:01:21.670
when we did slash todos slash ABC or 123,

04:01:22.540 --> 04:01:25.440
we have a delete method,
so that should all be good.

04:01:25.440 --> 04:01:29.040
Now let's see what happens
when we send that request.

04:01:30.715 --> 04:01:32.760
So we go to network, clear this,

04:01:32.760 --> 04:01:35.250
clear the console, and we delete the item.

04:01:37.120 --> 04:01:42.120
Interesting, we get a 404,
it says not found slash todos

04:01:43.050 --> 04:01:44.320
blah blah blah dot JSON.

04:01:45.630 --> 04:01:46.570
What is going on?

04:01:47.780 --> 04:01:48.810
Let's have a look.

04:01:50.960 --> 04:01:53.850
There's our requests
that ended up in a 404,

04:01:53.850 --> 04:01:57.450
but clearly we know that exists
because we just created it.

04:01:57.450 --> 04:01:59.030
And if we click on it,

04:02:00.460 --> 04:02:05.460
we notice that the
request method was "get".

04:02:07.200 --> 04:02:10.770
Now, why would it be "get"
when we specified "delete"

04:02:12.420 --> 04:02:14.120
in our method here?

04:02:14.120 --> 04:02:18.490
So unfortunately I have some
bad news and the bad news

04:02:18.490 --> 04:02:23.490
is that an HTML form only
supports get method or post.

04:02:25.160 --> 04:02:30.160
Very unfortunate for us
because we can not use delete.

04:02:31.400 --> 04:02:35.440
However we don't want to change our API

04:02:35.440 --> 04:02:38.630
and put all our code to
delete and update items

04:02:38.630 --> 04:02:41.030
into the post handler.

04:02:41.030 --> 04:02:43.480
Because if somebody were to build,

04:02:43.480 --> 04:02:46.450
let's say a mobile
application for our todo app,

04:02:47.370 --> 04:02:51.430
they would expect the REST API
to provide a delete endpoint.

04:02:52.400 --> 04:02:57.348
So this is really on us to
find a workaround for our web

04:02:57.348 --> 04:03:02.190
application so that we
can still make this work,

04:03:02.190 --> 04:03:06.710
but rely on the delete
endpoints, even though HTML forms

04:03:06.710 --> 04:03:08.010
don't actually support it.

04:03:09.890 --> 04:03:12.570
The way we can do that in SvelteKit

04:03:13.680 --> 04:03:15.150
is back in our todo-item.

04:03:16.060 --> 04:03:21.060
We have to conform to the post endpoint

04:03:21.290 --> 04:03:25.060
or post method because that's
the only thing we can do.

04:03:25.060 --> 04:03:26.970
So we'll change this to post,

04:03:28.450 --> 04:03:33.450
but we use a query parameter here,

04:03:33.500 --> 04:03:36.440
and that's just something
that we agree on.

04:03:36.440 --> 04:03:38.130
There's different ways
we could solve that.

04:03:38.130 --> 04:03:40.110
This is one way to do it.

04:03:40.110 --> 04:03:43.710
So what we say is that let's append

04:03:43.710 --> 04:03:48.710
