04:48:43.680 --> 04:48:45.880
Okay, what do we want to do now

04:48:45.880 --> 04:48:48.760
is leverage a feature from Svelte

04:48:48.760 --> 04:48:53.760
called actions in order
to enhance the HTML forms

04:48:53.870 --> 04:48:56.350
for visitors of our application

04:48:56.350 --> 04:48:57.880
that have JavaScript enabled.

04:48:59.000 --> 04:49:03.030
So we've got a new issue
called enhanced HTML forms.

04:49:03.030 --> 04:49:06.800
We start a new Gitpod workspace
for that specific task.

04:49:07.750 --> 04:49:12.600
And what we're going to do
now is basically find all the

04:49:12.600 --> 04:49:17.600
HTML forms that we have and
use this new Svelte action

04:49:18.420 --> 04:49:22.240
that we are going to
create that will help us

04:49:23.074 --> 04:49:28.074
to make an AJAX request
instead of a full page refresh.

04:49:28.230 --> 04:49:30.440
I'll show you what I mean by that.

04:49:30.440 --> 04:49:34.190
If we come here and we add a
new item currently by hitting

04:49:34.190 --> 04:49:38.820
enter here, you remember
it reloads the entire page.

04:49:38.820 --> 04:49:42.100
It adds the item, and then
redirect back to the homepage,

04:49:42.100 --> 04:49:46.930
which means it downloads
all the CSS, the HTML,

04:49:46.930 --> 04:49:47.780
and all the code.

04:49:48.740 --> 04:49:52.660
We really want to just
make an AJAX request

04:49:52.660 --> 04:49:57.660
to the endpoint, add the
item to our array in the API,

04:49:58.204 --> 04:50:00.670
and then update the UI accordingly.

04:50:02.130 --> 04:50:06.240
So the way we can do that
is by using Svelte actions.

04:50:08.711 --> 04:50:12.590
And Svelte actions are very powerful tool.

04:50:12.590 --> 04:50:17.270
Well-documented at Svelte.dev
but I'll walk you through

04:50:17.270 --> 04:50:19.150
and teach you everything you need to know.

04:50:21.050 --> 04:50:26.000
The first thing we want to
do is create a new action

04:50:26.000 --> 04:50:28.670
and an action is really just a function.

04:50:28.670 --> 04:50:29.820
So I like to have them

04:50:29.820 --> 04:50:34.810
under source lib, and then
in the actions directory,

04:50:34.810 --> 04:50:37.210
and in our case, we're
going to call it form.TS.

04:50:40.070 --> 04:50:44.893
So in here we just have
to export a function

04:50:44.893 --> 04:50:46.720
and the name of that function

04:50:46.720 --> 04:50:49.460
will become the name of our action.

04:50:49.460 --> 04:50:53.230
So export const, let's call this enhance

04:50:53.230 --> 04:50:55.540
because we will enhance the HTML form

04:50:55.540 --> 04:50:57.820
with additional functionality

04:50:59.620 --> 04:51:01.120
in case JavaScript is enabled.

04:51:03.010 --> 04:51:07.540
So it's a function and
that's basically it.

04:51:09.460 --> 04:51:10.520
Now with actions,

04:51:11.740 --> 04:51:16.370
there is a parameter being
passed to us by Svelte

04:51:16.370 --> 04:51:21.370
that represents the HTML element
that we use the action on.

04:51:24.090 --> 04:51:25.060
So in our case,

04:51:25.060 --> 04:51:29.940
we will use that enhance
action for HTML forms.

04:51:29.940 --> 04:51:33.260
So Svelte automatically passes us a form.

04:51:33.260 --> 04:51:38.260
And with TypeScript, we know
this is an HTML form element,

04:51:41.550 --> 04:51:45.650
and this is passed into
us into this action.

04:51:45.650 --> 04:51:49.150
So before we go any further,
let's see how we can use

04:51:49.150 --> 04:51:53.240
that in the code of our Svelte component,

04:51:53.240 --> 04:51:58.023
we copy the name and we
go to source roots index.

04:51:59.340 --> 04:52:02.610
And here in the top,

04:52:02.610 --> 04:52:04.610
we want to first import our new function

04:52:05.960 --> 04:52:07.770
or action, same thing.

04:52:07.770 --> 04:52:12.770
So import enhance from,

04:52:14.350 --> 04:52:19.007
and remember the shortcut
to go to a source lib.

04:52:20.430 --> 04:52:24.870
We can use the dollar sign lib slash,

04:52:24.870 --> 04:52:27.330
now we can see our new actions directory,

04:52:27.330 --> 04:52:30.510
and within that, the form file.

04:52:32.060 --> 04:52:36.010
Alrighty, with that we can go down

04:52:36.010 --> 04:52:39.150
and we'll start by enhancing the form

04:52:39.150 --> 04:52:42.060
to create a new todo-item.

04:52:43.590 --> 04:52:47.240
So we can use an action by saying use,

04:52:47.240 --> 04:52:49.910
and then the name of our action.

04:52:51.060 --> 04:52:54.400
As I mentioned Svelte provides a reference

04:52:54.400 --> 04:52:56.920
to the element we use the action on.

04:52:56.920 --> 04:53:00.820
So this is on the form element
and that's why the parameter

04:53:00.820 --> 04:53:05.820
we get is a form
parameter into our action.

04:53:06.750 --> 04:53:08.750
So let me show you what happens.

04:53:08.750 --> 04:53:09.740
Before we go any further,

04:53:09.740 --> 04:53:14.740
let's just do console log
action executed for example.

04:53:18.586 --> 04:53:23.586
If we switch to the UI
and we clear the console

04:53:24.900 --> 04:53:26.160
and we reload that page.

04:53:28.270 --> 04:53:29.150
You can see that

04:53:30.080 --> 04:53:34.360
as soon as the HTML form
gets mounted to the DOM,

04:53:35.380 --> 04:53:38.800
we can see that the action got executed.

04:53:39.990 --> 04:53:43.620
Okay, so now this means at that point,

04:53:43.620 --> 04:53:48.620
we can start to interact with
the form using JavaScript

04:53:48.710 --> 04:53:53.710
in our action to intercept
the submit request.

04:53:54.760 --> 04:53:57.490
And then instead of
doing a full page reload,

04:53:57.490 --> 04:54:01.700
we can just send an Ajax
request before we get there.

04:54:01.700 --> 04:54:02.750
I'm going to show you one more thing

04:54:02.750 --> 04:54:06.920
that is extremely important to
know when you build actions.

04:54:08.060 --> 04:54:10.190
And in order to do that,

04:54:10.190 --> 04:54:14.760
I'm going to rename that
text form mounted to DOM.

04:54:16.610 --> 04:54:18.650
Now, anything you do

04:54:18.650 --> 04:54:22.620
in the enhance function
here or in your action,

04:54:23.760 --> 04:54:27.420
keep in mind that this
action gets executed

04:54:27.420 --> 04:54:32.070
every time the HTML element
gets added to the DOM.

04:54:32.070 --> 04:54:35.220
So if we navigate from one page
to another and we come back,

04:54:36.080 --> 04:54:39.040
that enhanced function is called again.

04:54:39.040 --> 04:54:40.340
Let me demonstrate that

04:54:40.340 --> 04:54:44.090
so that we can then see a few things.

04:54:44.090 --> 04:54:45.750
I'm going to under source routes,

04:54:45.750 --> 04:54:48.330
I create a new file
called about-us.Svelte.

04:54:49.540 --> 04:54:54.093
And for now this just contains
an H1 element, about us,

04:54:55.770 --> 04:55:00.540
and a link that brings us back
to the homepage like that.

04:55:01.530 --> 04:55:05.990
And that will just move us back.

04:55:05.990 --> 04:55:09.160
On the index page itself under the title,

04:55:10.640 --> 04:55:12.990
I'm adding an anchor that
brings us to about us

04:55:13.940 --> 04:55:17.590
so we can navigate between
the two pages easily.

04:55:18.580 --> 04:55:21.210
All right, do that, clear things.

04:55:22.780 --> 04:55:23.730
We reload the page

04:55:25.290 --> 04:55:28.460
and you can see that the
form is mounted to the DOM.

04:55:29.670 --> 04:55:32.090
And now, oh there we go,

04:55:32.090 --> 04:55:35.640
had to refresh, hot module
reloading kicked in.

04:55:37.160 --> 04:55:38.250
So it got mounted to the DOM.

04:55:38.250 --> 04:55:43.250
And now if we click the about
us, we load the about us page,

04:55:43.880 --> 04:55:44.780
and if we go back,

04:55:46.520 --> 04:55:50.210
you can see that the form
mounted to DOM appears again.

04:55:51.550 --> 04:55:53.140
This is extremely important to know,

04:55:53.140 --> 04:55:57.170
because anything we do in our action

04:55:59.014 --> 04:56:04.014
happens every time the HTML
element gets added to the DOM.

04:56:04.160 --> 04:56:05.480
So navigating between back and forth,

04:56:05.480 --> 04:56:09.040
we have to somehow clean up
everything we do in here.

04:56:09.040 --> 04:56:11.300
For example if we were to add

04:56:11.300 --> 04:56:14.201
an event listener or create something

04:56:14.201 --> 04:56:18.490
in memory or whatever,
we'll have to clean that up

04:56:18.490 --> 04:56:22.930
when the HTML form gets
removed from the DOM.

04:56:22.930 --> 04:56:25.800
So when we navigate away from the page or

04:56:25.800 --> 04:56:28.800
the element gets removed from
the DOM, for any other reason.

04:56:30.710 --> 04:56:32.890
To do that, the convention
is that we can return

04:56:32.890 --> 04:56:37.890
an object from our action that
contains a destroy function.

04:56:39.460 --> 04:56:42.830
And in that destroy function, we can

04:56:45.010 --> 04:56:49.563
print form removed from DOM.

04:56:51.950 --> 04:56:55.393
And now if we have a look at the console,

04:56:59.350 --> 04:57:00.450
when we load the page,

04:57:02.010 --> 04:57:04.130
you can see the form, mounted to the DOM.

04:57:05.080 --> 04:57:09.840
When we navigate away, the
form was removed from the DOM.

04:57:09.840 --> 04:57:13.280
And then when we come back,
the form is mounted again.

04:57:14.480 --> 04:57:17.050
So anything we do in the action,

04:57:17.050 --> 04:57:22.050
it is very important that we
undo, you know, in air quotes,

04:57:22.610 --> 04:57:25.150
everything we did so that
we have no memory leaks,

04:57:25.150 --> 04:57:30.050
and we don't accidentally add
multiple like event listeners.

04:57:30.050 --> 04:57:33.330
And then all of a sudden our
code executes multiple times,

04:57:33.330 --> 04:57:34.180
things like that.

04:57:35.800 --> 04:57:37.650
So with that knowledge in mind,

04:57:37.650 --> 04:57:40.910
let's have a look at
what we really want to do

04:57:40.910 --> 04:57:45.860
in order to make the user
experience a bit better

04:57:45.860 --> 04:57:47.650
for people with JavaScript enabled.

04:57:48.870 --> 04:57:52.640
When somebody actually,
before we do that, hold on,

04:57:52.640 --> 04:57:55.780
let's clean this up, we
don't need the about us page.

04:57:57.700 --> 04:58:00.710
And in our index file, we
