06:18:16.400 --> 06:18:20.750
that Prisma Migrate dev
command automatically runs

06:18:20.750 --> 06:18:24.800
before we start our SvelteKit application.

06:18:26.050 --> 06:18:27.250
So that's an easy fix.

06:18:28.610 --> 06:18:31.010
All we need to do is open
the package.json file.

06:18:31.940 --> 06:18:33.390
We already have a dev script.

06:18:34.330 --> 06:18:38.000
Now in order to run something
before the dev script,

06:18:39.210 --> 06:18:41.030
we can either come here and say,

06:18:43.717 --> 06:18:46.480
prisma migrate dev &amp;&amp; Svelte-Kit dev.

06:18:47.640 --> 06:18:49.296
However if we want to run more commands

06:18:49.296 --> 06:18:51.288
before we start the dev server,

06:18:51.288 --> 06:18:54.590
this starts to get really
hard to understand.

06:18:54.590 --> 06:18:57.390
So here's a little
trick that NPM provides.

06:18:58.300 --> 06:19:03.300
We can take that and then
take the name of our command

06:19:05.930 --> 06:19:10.830
and create a new command
or a new script called pre

06:19:10.830 --> 06:19:14.250
and the name of this one
here, let me show you,

06:19:14.250 --> 06:19:19.250
in this case, we are talking
about, we want a dev script.

06:19:19.870 --> 06:19:21.940
We want to run something
before the dev script runs.

06:19:21.940 --> 06:19:23.620
So we can say predev,

06:19:24.710 --> 06:19:28.940
which means it runs before the dev script.

06:19:28.940 --> 06:19:31.610
And we wanna run prisma migrate dev.

06:19:32.860 --> 06:19:36.200
This is nothing, you know, no matching,

06:19:36.200 --> 06:19:39.850
that's just a regular NPM feature.

06:19:40.760 --> 06:19:45.210
And with that now every time
we start our dev server,

06:19:45.210 --> 06:19:50.210
if we came here and ran
NPM run dev, we hit editor,

06:19:50.480 --> 06:19:53.580
you can see that Prisma
Migrate dev runs first.

06:19:54.810 --> 06:19:57.740
And then it starts to development server

06:19:57.740 --> 06:19:59.640
and our application is up and running.

