06:50:19.290 --> 06:50:24.290
And what we now need to do
is in the package.json file,

06:50:28.160 --> 06:50:31.870
you remember, in development,

06:50:32.980 --> 06:50:35.920
before we start the dev server,

06:50:35.920 --> 06:50:39.740
we created a predev script

06:50:39.740 --> 06:50:44.060
where we run the prisma
migrate dev command.

06:50:44.060 --> 06:50:48.720
This helps ensure that
the Postgres database

06:50:48.720 --> 06:50:52.200
is always up to date with
the latest migrations

06:50:52.200 --> 06:50:55.390
that exists under Prisma migrations.

06:50:55.390 --> 06:50:58.510
Now this, as the command says

06:50:58.510 --> 06:51:02.910
is for development, but when
we deploy to production,

06:51:02.910 --> 06:51:06.080
there might be changes
to the database schema

06:51:06.080 --> 06:51:09.840
that we have to apply to the
production database as well.

06:51:09.840 --> 06:51:14.840
And in that case, we don't
want to run Prisma migrate dev.

06:51:15.990 --> 06:51:20.990
We want to run a production
level command for that.

06:51:21.210 --> 06:51:24.200
Now, when do we want to run that command?

06:51:24.200 --> 06:51:26.130
When we deploy to Vercel,

06:51:27.360 --> 06:51:32.070
the Vercel adapter for
SvelteKit will automatically

06:51:32.070 --> 06:51:36.080
execute the build script.

06:51:36.080 --> 06:51:38.720
So, or in other words,

06:51:38.720 --> 06:51:42.010
Vercel will actually
execute the build script

06:51:42.010 --> 06:51:46.550
and the SvelteKit command
line interface here,

06:51:46.550 --> 06:51:50.643
that will then execute the Vercel adapter

06:51:50.643 --> 06:51:52.270
and deploy the application.

06:51:52.270 --> 06:51:54.810
And we'll talk about
that when we deploy the

06:51:54.810 --> 06:51:59.810
web application, but the build
script is something where

06:52:02.419 --> 06:52:05.557
we want to run that command

06:52:06.610 --> 06:52:10.370
to update the database and migrate

06:52:10.370 --> 06:52:12.010
if there are any migrations.

06:52:13.340 --> 06:52:17.950
The problem is we could run
that build script in our

06:52:17.950 --> 06:52:22.330
local environment as well,
so this would be confusing.

06:52:22.330 --> 06:52:25.140
We wouldn't want to update the database

06:52:25.140 --> 06:52:27.390
by running the build script locally.

06:52:27.390 --> 06:52:32.050
So luckily there is a
script that we can leverage.

06:52:32.050 --> 06:52:35.420
So if we add a new script
to our package.json file,

06:52:35.420 --> 06:52:37.780
and we call it vercel-build.

06:52:40.220 --> 06:52:45.220
This script is only executed
when we deploy to Vercel.

06:52:45.730 --> 06:52:47.430
And at that time,

06:52:47.430 --> 06:52:51.410
this is the perfect place
to upgrade our database.

06:52:52.330 --> 06:52:54.820
The way we do it is we use Prisma,

06:52:56.320 --> 06:53:00.760
prisma migrate, just like
we did in the predev script,

06:53:01.910 --> 06:53:05.770
but instead of dev, we use deploy

06:53:07.280 --> 06:53:11.910
and then once that's done
and the database is updated,

06:53:14.064 --> 06:53:17.880
we can say &amp;&amp; npm run build.

06:53:19.100 --> 06:53:23.660
So that Vercel then kicks in,
first deploys the database

06:53:23.660 --> 06:53:27.740
and then runs the build script
for the web application.

06:53:29.580 --> 06:53:33.460
So let's quickly run that build script.

06:53:33.460 --> 06:53:37.160
So the one we're going to
execute here npm run build,

06:53:37.160 --> 06:53:40.290
let's run that in our environment

06:53:40.290 --> 06:53:44.300
to see what actually happens
when we deploy to Vercel.

06:53:45.410 --> 06:53:46.590
So npm run build.

06:53:52.630 --> 06:53:55.990
And it is now telling us
that it could not detect

06:53:55.990 --> 06:53:58.180
a supported production environment.

06:53:58.180 --> 06:54:02.620
And that's because we are not
actually running on Vercel.

06:54:02.620 --> 06:54:07.620
So because in our Svelte config,
we use that adapter-auto,

06:54:08.880 --> 06:54:12.930
it tries to determine
where we are executing

06:54:12.930 --> 06:54:14.950
this command from.

06:54:14.950 --> 06:54:19.100
And because it doesn't see
this environment as being

06:54:19.100 --> 06:54:24.100
Vercel, it automatically
basically gives us that error.

06:54:25.090 --> 06:54:28.920
Now I spend a lot of time in
