06:54:37.960 --> 06:54:41.020
And then we run that and
NPM run build script again,

06:54:42.670 --> 06:54:45.170
it goes through the same steps

06:54:46.633 --> 06:54:50.150
and now it determined
that we are on Vercel.

06:54:50.150 --> 06:54:54.240
So we basically just, you
know, cheated a little bit,

06:54:54.240 --> 06:54:57.090
but this is only temporary because I want

06:54:57.090 --> 06:55:01.180
to show you what happens on Vercel.

06:55:01.180 --> 06:55:03.110
So the first thing we
noticed is that he created

06:55:03.110 --> 06:55:06.880
a new directory called
.vercel_build_output,

06:55:07.790 --> 06:55:12.790
and within that directory, we
have a functions sub-directory

06:55:16.070 --> 06:55:18.190
and then node, and then render.

06:55:19.060 --> 06:55:24.060
So that index file here
within the render directory,

06:55:24.180 --> 06:55:29.180
this is our generated
code, it's very long,

06:55:31.340 --> 06:55:35.850
but that's basically our
generated code for the application

06:55:35.850 --> 06:55:39.340
that we developed, our
service side application.

06:55:40.320 --> 06:55:44.480
Now, when we deploy to production

06:55:45.530 --> 06:55:47.590
in that directory here,

06:55:47.590 --> 06:55:52.180
we need to include our schema.prisma file,

06:55:56.182 --> 06:55:59.730
that needs to be available
so that when we run

06:55:59.730 --> 06:56:04.710
Prisma migrate deploy,
Prisma can find the schema,

06:56:04.710 --> 06:56:06.190
and in the schema, you'll remember,

06:56:06.190 --> 06:56:10.370
it has the information on how
to connect to the database,

06:56:10.370 --> 06:56:13.600
