07:04:29.850 --> 07:04:34.720
The reason for that is that
in the Svelte config file,

07:04:36.070 --> 07:04:39.700
we have an adapter that is being imported

07:04:39.700 --> 07:04:44.570
that's called adapter-auto,
and that is used here.

07:04:44.570 --> 07:04:45.900
As you recall, from the very beginning,

07:04:45.900 --> 07:04:50.900
adapters are used by SvelteKit
to prepare the application

07:04:51.630 --> 07:04:54.180
for the different environments.

07:04:54.180 --> 07:04:57.960
So if you deploy to Netlify CloudFlare

07:04:57.960 --> 07:05:00.040
or Vercel at this point in time,

07:05:00.880 --> 07:05:04.210
then you don't have to
make any code changes.

07:05:04.210 --> 07:05:08.210
If you're curious what the
latest supported environments are

07:05:08.210 --> 07:05:10.980
head over to kit.svelte.dev/docs,

07:05:12.960 --> 07:05:16.880
scroll down in the navigation

07:05:16.880 --> 07:05:19.130
until you get to adapters

07:05:19.130 --> 07:05:22.410
where it says supported environment,

07:05:22.410 --> 07:05:27.410
and you have a list here
of supported environments.

07:05:27.540 --> 07:05:31.150
So the three are here, we
are deploying to Vercel.

07:05:31.150 --> 07:05:33.890
So we are in luck and we don't have

07:05:33.890 --> 07:05:36.220
to actually make any code changes.

07:05:36.220 --> 07:05:40.420
The only thing we have
to do is log into Vercel.

07:05:41.360 --> 07:05:45.380
So make sure we create an
account, pick the right team,

07:05:45.380 --> 07:05:47.650
and then you can say new project.

07:05:49.270 --> 07:05:52.820
And from the screen,

07:05:52.820 --> 07:05:57.820
