we want to configure,

07:06:27.940 --> 07:06:30.837
which is our DATABASE_URL

07:06:30.837 --> 07:06:34.430
that we configured locally or on Gitpod

07:06:35.620 --> 07:06:37.940
as part of the developer environment.

07:06:40.073 --> 07:06:43.950
In production, we also have
to specify a DATABASE_URL,

07:06:46.770 --> 07:06:50.970
so that Prisma knows how
to connect to the database.

07:06:50.970 --> 07:06:54.810
The value that we want to add here

07:06:54.810 --> 07:06:56.930
comes from the Railway.app,

07:06:57.780 --> 07:07:02.470
remember we created a
Postgres database here

07:07:02.470 --> 07:07:05.430
and it has a Postgres connection URL.

07:07:05.430 --> 07:07:06.630
So we want to copy that.

07:07:07.510 --> 07:07:12.510
And over in Vercel at
this as the DATABASE_URL,

07:07:13.760 --> 07:07:16.710
we say add, and with that,

07:07:16.710 --> 07:07:21.260
that environment variable is
available for Prisma to pick up

07:07:21.260 --> 07:07:23.130
and we then can say deploy.

07:07:25.920 --> 07:07:28.040
And you can see down here,

07:07:28.040 --> 07:07:31.390
it starts to build four seconds ago.

07:07:32.950 --> 07:07:36.090
It's running all the necessary scripts

07:07:36.090 --> 07:07:40.790
in order to build the
SvelteKit application.

07:07:40.790 --> 07:07:45.490
It will also run the post
build scripts that we specified

07:07:45.490 --> 07:07:50.490
so that the database
will be populated with

07:07:50.640 --> 07:07:55.640
the table that is needed as
well as all the other things

07:07:56.080 --> 07:07:59.520
that are necessary to make this work.

07:07:59.520 --> 07:08:00.900
Lots going on.

07:08:00.900 --> 07:08:05.890
We can see here that one
migration found in the migrations.

07:08:05.890 --> 07:08:07.850
So it applies that.

07:08:07.850 --> 07:08:10.200
This is happening because we specified

07:08:10.200 --> 07:08:14.580
that Vercel build script, which
runs Prisma migrate deploy.

07:08:16.380 --> 07:08:18.080
So this is why it said, Hey,

07:08:18.080 --> 07:08:22.180
I'm running this migration
and applied to the database.

07:08:23.030 --> 07:08:24.740
It does a bunch of other stuff.

07:08:24.740 --> 07:08:27.730
There's two warnings we can
safely ignore that's okay.

07:08:28.570 --> 07:08:33.010
And eventually we are
uploading the build cache

07:08:34.409 --> 07:08:36.220
to the server.

07:08:36.220 --> 07:08:39.700
And I have seen this page getting stuck

07:08:40.610 --> 07:08:43.720
