07:09:53.750 --> 07:09:55.150
Let's do that one more time.

07:09:56.740 --> 07:09:57.830
There we go.

07:09:57.830 --> 07:10:02.750
And now we have the first
item added to the database.

07:10:02.750 --> 07:10:07.750
If we head over to Railway
and we select the data tab

07:10:08.250 --> 07:10:12.620
in our Postgres database,
we can see that Prisma

07:10:12.620 --> 07:10:16.230
created a migrations table, that's okay.

07:10:16.230 --> 07:10:19.670
Prisma will manage that,
nothing for us to worry about.

07:10:19.670 --> 07:10:22.740
More importantly we can see the todo table

07:10:22.740 --> 07:10:27.630
that now contains our first todo item.

07:10:27.630 --> 07:10:30.520
If we were to go back to production,

07:10:30.520 --> 07:10:34.420
