07:12:51.600 --> 07:12:54.210
Let's quickly recap what we've done

07:12:54.210 --> 07:12:58.470
and how you can move on and
do more features, development

07:12:58.470 --> 07:13:01.660
on that, or add other things
you might be interested in.

07:13:02.780 --> 07:13:07.780
First off we created a
user interface with Svelte

07:13:07.810 --> 07:13:11.411
that was really the basic foundation

07:13:11.411 --> 07:13:13.380
that we needed for the web app

07:13:13.380 --> 07:13:17.000
in order to create
todo-items, update them,

07:13:17.000 --> 07:13:18.720
delete them and display all of it.

07:13:19.970 --> 07:13:24.970
We then moved on and created
a SvelteKit backend API.

07:13:25.530 --> 07:13:27.640
There was a REST API with endpoints

07:13:27.640 --> 07:13:31.650
to create, read, update,
and delete todo-items.

07:13:32.510 --> 07:13:37.510
We used REST or HTTP to
connect to that backend

07:13:37.780 --> 07:13:41.640
and returned JSON data
to display in the UI.

07:13:42.560 --> 07:13:44.890
At the very beginning,
we started off building

07:13:44.890 --> 07:13:49.530
that application with JavaScript disabled.

07:13:49.530 --> 07:13:52.450
So we used the regular HTML form elements

07:13:52.450 --> 07:13:56.030
and post requests to submit the data.

07:13:56.030 --> 07:14:01.030
We then enhanced our
forms with Svelte actions,

07:14:01.620 --> 07:14:06.620
which allows us to intercept
the HTML form submission,

07:14:07.260 --> 07:14:10.210
and instead do an Ajax request.

07:14:10.210 --> 07:14:12.270
So we don't have to reload the entire page

07:14:12.270 --> 07:14:14.410
for every action that we do.

07:14:14.410 --> 07:14:17.560
So we now have a front end
that works with JavaScript.

07:14:17.560 --> 07:14:20.410
It also works with no JavaScript
enabled in the browser.

07:14:22.150 --> 07:14:24.500
In the second part of the course,

07:14:24.500 --> 07:14:28.250
we went ahead and used Prisma,

07:14:30.670 --> 07:14:33.980
an ORM to let us connect
to a Postgres database.

07:14:33.980 --> 07:14:37.900
This really simplified the
entire integration with

07:14:37.900 --> 07:14:42.900
the database, we did not write
a single line of SQL code.

07:14:43.560 --> 07:14:48.040
All we really did was
using generated TypeScript

07:14:48.040 --> 07:14:51.840
and JavaScript in order to
connect to the database,

07:14:51.840 --> 07:14:53.380
we were reading data,

07:14:53.380 --> 07:14:56.870
updating data all by simply
just calling functions

07:14:56.870 --> 07:15:00.150
within our JavaScript
and TypeScript files.

07:15:01.290 --> 07:15:04.200
Lastly when we had all this working

07:15:04.200 --> 07:15:06.060
in a developer environment,

07:15:06.060 --> 07:15:10.460
we then deployed the web
application to Vercel

07:15:10.460 --> 07:15:13.790
and we deployed the Postgres
database to Railway.app

07:15:14.950 --> 07:15:18.300
where it is now running
so that we can connect

07:15:18.300 --> 07:15:20.200
to it from our production environment.

07:15:21.510 --> 07:15:24.410
When we developed the project,

07:15:24.410 --> 07:15:29.410
we did all of that in a
Gitpod developer environment.

07:15:29.690 --> 07:15:33.830
So you notice that for every
task that we worked on,

07:15:33.830 --> 07:15:36.520
we started a new GitPod workspace.

07:15:36.520 --> 07:15:38.230
And this is the concept

07:15:38.230 --> 07:15:43.140
of what ephemeral developer
environments or are all about.

07:15:43.140 --> 07:15:45.870
You start in an environment,
it's fully automated,

07:15:45.870 --> 07:15:49.810
it started our developer
server, installed dependencies,

07:15:49.810 --> 07:15:53.380
and we then basically
could just write our code,

07:15:53.380 --> 07:15:56.040
stop the environment,
and for the next task,

07:15:56.040 --> 07:15:59.440
we opened a new environment to
do the work we wanted to do.

07:16:01.550 --> 07:16:04.510
Amazing achievement,
congratulations, once again,

07:16:04.510 --> 07:16:08.610
this is a full stack
application that you can use

07:16:08.610 --> 07:16:11.800
as a foundation to do further work

07:16:11.800 --> 07:16:13.400
and build your own projects.

07:16:16.490 --> 07:16:19.760
Let's spend a few minutes
talking about what's next.

07:16:20.790 --> 07:16:24.770
How can you further enhance
the application in order to

07:16:24.770 --> 07:16:28.380
deepen your knowledge about
the technologies that we used

07:16:28.380 --> 07:16:31.920
and the different
providers where we deployed

07:16:31.920 --> 07:16:33.920
the application as well as the database?

07:16:34.760 --> 07:16:37.610
The first thing I want to bring
up as a suggestion to look

07:16:37.610 --> 07:16:41.710
into is trying to deploy
the web application

07:16:41.710 --> 07:16:45.570
and the API endpoints to a
different hosting provider.

07:16:45.570 --> 07:16:49.300
As part of the course, we used
Vercel and I introduced you

07:16:49.300 --> 07:16:52.670
to the adaptor concept of SvelteKit.

07:16:52.670 --> 07:16:57.320
So an easy kind of next steps
would be to maybe deploy this

07:16:57.320 --> 07:17:02.320
entire application to Netlify
or CloudFlare or any other

07:17:02.890 --> 07:17:05.700
hosting provider that you
might be familiar with.

07:17:05.700 --> 07:17:09.050
So this would be a good next steps,

07:17:09.050 --> 07:17:12.460
minimal code changes in
order to get it resolved.

07:17:12.460 --> 07:17:17.420
So you would get some quick
success by looking into this.

07:17:18.910 --> 07:17:23.160
Another suggestion would be to play around

07:17:25.020 --> 07:17:26.600
and try to use a different database.

07:17:26.600 --> 07:17:29.380
Maybe you are not familiar with Postgres.

07:17:29.380 --> 07:17:31.910
Maybe you are more familiar with MySQL,

07:17:32.750 --> 07:17:37.750
try to change the database
to MySQL instead of Postgres.

07:17:40.103 --> 07:17:43.050
Read up about the Prisma configuration,

07:17:43.050 --> 07:17:45.340
how you can change that and, you know,

07:17:45.340 --> 07:17:48.520
try Railway or try Planet Scale

07:17:48.520 --> 07:17:50.500
or any other database provider.

07:17:50.500 --> 07:17:54.900
See if we can connect the
API to that database system

07:17:54.900 --> 07:17:58.880
and learn about that part
of the backend development

07:17:58.880 --> 07:17:59.930
in this entire stack.

07:18:01.100 --> 07:18:03.172
Lastly, a third suggestion

07:18:03.172 --> 07:18:08.172
to look into might be
to enhance the project.

07:18:08.410 --> 07:18:12.050
Right now, this is a very
